{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the thing was good in my eyes.</b> Meaning, according to the reason you said ״וְיַחְפְּרוּ לָנוּ״, and they of blessed memory said (Yalkut Shimoni Shelach) that the intention is that the spies would be sent to see the hiding-places in which the Canaanites bury their money. And the verse's saying <b>in my eyes</b> means: I, who have eyes of flesh — but in the eyes of the Searcher of hearts, not. And see what I wrote in parashat Shelach (Numbers 13:2)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:16.956159555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}